fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Loss of heterozygosity in normal cell clones demonstrated by amplification of microsatellites D17s1323 (<bold>A</bold>) and D13s267 (<bold>B</bold>). The normal tissue control for each sample shows two allele peaks. The &#x02018;normal' clones from samples 3 and 4 each demonstrate loss of one allele (arrow).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="95-6603298f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">The number of LOHs detected in samples of &#x02018;normal' human breast tissue from two mastectomies and two prophylactic mastectomies</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Sample no.</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Specimen</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of clones</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of informative microsatellite markers</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of LOH</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>&#x00025; of clones with LOH</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Mastectomy BRCA2</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">199</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2 wt</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.005</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Prophylactic BRCA1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">197</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">6</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2 wt</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.015</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">3</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Mastectomy BRCA1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">406</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">6</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">2 wt, 1 mut</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.739</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">4</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Prophylactic BRCA1 (contralateral to sample 3)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">190</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">6</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">1 wt, 1 mut, 1 non-BRCA1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.579</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label/><p>Wt&#x0003d;loss from wild-type allele, mut&#x0003d;loss from mutant allele.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>